"Historical Knowledge Centres" by Lattice Reconstruction Agents

The story headline is "Evidence-aware reconstruction environments".

An evidence state is a kind of value. The evidence states are attested, reconstructed, hypothetical, disputed, and unknown.

A room has an evidence state. The evidence state of a room is usually reconstructed.
A thing has an evidence state. The evidence state of a thing is usually reconstructed.
A room has some text called the evidence note.
A thing has some text called the evidence note.

The Reconstruction Hub is a room. "Six historical knowledge centres can be approached from here. This hub is navigation, not an assertion that the institutions were physically connected. Type UGARIT, NINEVEH, ALEXANDRIA, NALANDA, SINAI, or BAGHDAD. Type EVIDENCE anywhere to inspect the epistemic status of your present location."

The player is in the Reconstruction Hub.

Evidence-checking is an action applying to nothing.
Understand "evidence" or "uncertainty" as evidence-checking.
Carry out evidence-checking:
	say "Evidence state: [evidence state of the location].[paragraph break][evidence note of the location]".

Operations-indexing is an action applying to nothing.
Understand "help" or "commands" or "index" or "operations" as operations-indexing.
Carry out operations-indexing:
	say "LRA OPERATIONS INDEX[paragraph break]UGARIT · NINEVEH · ALEXANDRIA · NALANDA · SINAI · BAGHDAD — enter a knowledge centre.[line break]HUB — return to the Reconstruction Hub.[line break]EVIDENCE / UNCERTAINTY — inspect the evidence state of your current location.[line break]LOOK — inspect the current location.[line break]Compass directions such as NORTH, SOUTH, EAST, and WEST — move where a local exit exists.[paragraph break]Only meaningful routes exist in each reconstruction. Context-sensitive operations will be added next.".

Hub-returning is an action applying to nothing.
Understand "hub" or "libraries" as hub-returning.
Carry out hub-returning:
	move the player to the Reconstruction Hub, without printing a room description;
	try looking.

Ugarit-going is an action applying to nothing.
Understand "ugarit" as Ugarit-going.
Carry out Ugarit-going: move the player to the Ugarit City Context, without printing a room description; try looking.

Nineveh-going is an action applying to nothing.
Understand "nineveh" as Nineveh-going.
Carry out Nineveh-going: move the player to the Nineveh City Context, without printing a room description; try looking.

Alexandria-going is an action applying to nothing.
Understand "alexandria" as Alexandria-going.
Carry out Alexandria-going: move the player to the Alexandria Evidence Threshold, without printing a room description; try looking.

Nalanda-going is an action applying to nothing.
Understand "nalanda" as Nalanda-going.
Carry out Nalanda-going: move the player to the Nalanda Mahavihara Context, without printing a room description; try looking.

Sinai-going is an action applying to nothing.
Understand "sinai" or "saint catherine's" or "saint catherine" as Sinai-going.
Carry out Sinai-going: move the player to the Saint Catherine's Monastery Context, without printing a room description; try looking.

Baghdad-going is an action applying to nothing.
Understand "baghdad" or "bayt al-hikma" or "house of wisdom" as Baghdad-going.
Carry out Baghdad-going: move the player to the Baghdad Evidence Threshold, without printing a room description; try looking.

Section - Ugarit

The Ugarit City Context is a room. "Late Bronze Age Ugarit is represented as a city containing multiple archival contexts rather than a single 'Great Library'. From here you can enter the ROYAL ZONE or the ACROPOLIS CONTEXT. The exact ancient function of individual findspots must not be inferred from the presence of tablets." The evidence state of the Ugarit City Context is attested. The evidence note is "High confidence: Ugarit/Ras Shamra, its urban sectors, and multiple archival findspots are archaeologically attested. Exact furnishing and original room use are not reconstructed without evidence."

The Ugarit Royal Zone is north of the Ugarit City Context. "A schematic palace-sector reconstruction. Tablet recovery contexts may be explored, but no shelving, desks, baskets, or ancient filing system is supplied without direct evidence." The evidence state of the Ugarit Royal Zone is reconstructed. The evidence note is "The royal palace and tablet finds are attested; this navigable spatial simplification is a reconstruction."

The Ugarit Acropolis Context is east of the Ugarit City Context. "Religious and elite contexts on the acropolis include tablet findspots. A findspot is not automatically an original archive room." The evidence state of the Ugarit Acropolis Context is reconstructed. The evidence note is "Sector and tablet evidence is strong; room function and original storage arrangements remain qualified or unknown."

Section - Nineveh

The Nineveh City Context is a room. "Nineveh contains palace contexts associated with the surviving tablet corpus. The collection is not represented as one freestanding library building. NORTH leads toward the Southwest Palace recovery context; EAST toward the North Palace context." The evidence state of the Nineveh City Context is attested. The evidence note is "Nineveh, the palaces, and the tablet corpus are strongly attested. Surviving modern collections do not preserve a perfect map of original placement."

The Southwest Palace Recovery Context is north of the Nineveh City Context. "Rooms conventionally numbered 40 and 41 are important excavation recovery contexts. Their excavation labels do not by themselves prove purpose-built library-room functions." The evidence state of the Southwest Palace Recovery Context is attested. The evidence note is "Recovery from the Southwest Palace is attested. Precise pre-destruction distribution and furniture are not."

The North Palace Recovery Context is east of the Nineveh City Context. "The North Palace, including the excavation context known as Room C, yielded tablets. Modern identifiers and fragment joins can be explored without pretending they reproduce an ancient catalogue." The evidence state of the North Palace Recovery Context is attested. The evidence note is "Palace and recovery contexts are attested; original arrangement is incompletely recoverable."

Section - Alexandria

The Alexandria Evidence Threshold is a room. "The Library of Alexandria is historically attested, but no definitive archaeological building or floor plan survives. NORTH enters an intentionally ABSTRACT scholarly reconstruction. No invented monumental library plan is presented as fact." The evidence state of the Alexandria Evidence Threshold is disputed. The evidence note is "Moderate confidence in the institution and bibliographic activity; low confidence in architecture, precise location, collection scale, and destruction narrative."

The Ptolemaic Scholarly Reconstruction is north of the Alexandria Evidence Threshold. "This is an interpretive space for the Mouseion-associated scholarly institution, royal patronage, papyrus culture, and Callimachan bibliographic activity. It is not a recovered room." The evidence state of the Ptolemaic Scholarly Reconstruction is hypothetical. The evidence note is "Interpretive reconstruction only. Exact architecture, room count, entrance, shelving and collection arrangement are unknown."

Section - Nalanda

The Nalanda Mahavihara Context is a room. "Nalanda is represented first as an excavated monastic and scholastic complex, not as a legendary standalone library. NORTH leads to a monastic court; EAST to a scholastic activity space." The evidence state of the Nalanda Mahavihara Context is attested. The evidence note is "Excavated monasteries, temples, walls, cells, courts and circulation are strongly supported. Assignment of an excavated building as 'the library' is not established here."

The Nalanda Monastic Court is north of the Nalanda Mahavihara Context. "A schematic navigable court derived from the character of the excavated monastic complexes. It does not assign manuscript storage to an unattested room." The evidence state of the Nalanda Monastic Court is reconstructed. The evidence note is "Monastic courts are archaeologically attested; this particular navigable simplification is reconstructed."

The Nalanda Scholastic Space is east of the Nalanda Mahavihara Context. "Study, teaching and debate belong to the institution's documented scholastic history. Manuscript use may be discussed, but no legendary manuscript count or invented shelf arrangement is supplied." The evidence state of the Nalanda Scholastic Space is reconstructed. The evidence note is "Scholastic activity is historically supported; exact activity placement within this reconstructed space is not."

Section - Saint Catherine's

The Saint Catherine's Monastery Context is a room. "A living monastery and manuscript-preserving institution, not a ruin-state fiction. NORTH leads toward the manuscript collection context. Historical room arrangements vary through time and are not flattened into one unchanged library." The evidence state of the Saint Catherine's Monastery Context is attested. The evidence note is "Standing fabric, institutional continuity, manuscript corpus and modern cataloguing provide unusually strong evidence. Historical room-by-room arrangement still requires date-specific evidence."

The Saint Catherine's Manuscript Context is north of the Saint Catherine's Monastery Context. "Codices and their modern documentation can be represented individually when sourced. Generic ancient shelving or an unchanged fifteen-century library room is not assumed." The evidence state of the Saint Catherine's Manuscript Context is reconstructed. The evidence note is "The manuscript corpus is strongly attested. This generic navigable collection context does not claim to reproduce one historical room."

Section - Baghdad

The Baghdad Evidence Threshold is a room. "Bayt al-Hikma is approached through textual and historiographical evidence. Its precise site and architecture are not securely reconstructed here. NORTH enters an abstract royal-collection hypothesis space." The evidence state of the Baghdad Evidence Threshold is disputed. The evidence note is "The named institution has textual support, but its character, departments, architecture, precise location, staffing and public access are debated or unknown."

The Bayt al-Hikma Hypothesis Space is north of the Baghdad Evidence Threshold. "An explicitly hypothetical environment for examining claims about a royal collection and scholarly activity in Abbasid Baghdad. It is not presented as the recovered House of Wisdom building." The evidence state of the Bayt al-Hikma Hypothesis Space is hypothetical. The evidence note is "No secure floor plan or archaeological building identification is asserted. Observatory attachment, universal academy structure and invented departments are excluded."

When play begins:
	say "HISTORICAL KNOWLEDGE CENTRES // reconstruction network[paragraph break]";
	say "This simulation separates attested evidence from reconstruction and hypothesis.[paragraph break]";
	say "Type a site name to enter it; type HUB to return; type EVIDENCE to inspect uncertainty. Type HELP for the operations index.[paragraph break]".
